From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:15:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Configure build for GrapheneOS GSI: apps and packages

Adapt the AOSP build configuration for GrapheneOS GSI:

- Replace generic webview module with TrichromeWebView (Vanadium)
- Use GrapheneOS TrichromeChrome as browser (replaces Browser2)
- Remove QuickSearchBox (not in GrapheneOS)
- Remove Camera and Messaging from GSI product -- users install from
  GrapheneOS App Store to save system image space
- Remove packages that are not useful or not desired in GSI builds:
  Calendar (deprecated, CalendarProvider kept), MusicFX, Auditor
  (requires hardware attestation), PdfViewerGOS, InfoApp,
  DeviceDiagnostics, EasterEgg, HardeningTestApp, LiveWallpapersPicker
  (deprecated), PhotoTable, WallpaperPickerGOS, ContactsGOS (use AOSP
  Contacts), BluetoothViewerGOS, TalkBackGOS (use standard TalkBack
  included in handheld_product.mk), GrapheneOS Updater (only useful for
  official GrapheneOS devices)
- Remove LogViewer from GSI system image
- Exclude AOSP sample APN list from GSI build
- Use the GrapheneOS Messaging soong module name (external/Messaging)
  in gsi/Android.bp so aosp_system_image does not depend on an
  undefined module, which fails soong bootstrap

Combines the former 'Configure build for GrapheneOS GSI: apps and
packages' and 'Use GrapheneOS Messaging module name in GSI system
image' patches.
